{
  "dom_id": "step-q343184",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14096050/assets/e0c966c29904cd5b5bce39e8a6675f05b658c457fa58338f336b90ee50c9141b.png)\n\nA factory uses a rectangular mold with a fixed width of $18\\,\\text{in}$ and a fixed height of $10\\,\\text{in}.$ Liquid resin is poured in so that the resin fills the mold and the length increases as the front face moves. What is the rate of change of the length if the volume is increasing at a rate of $540\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}/\\text{min}?$\n\nThe length is increasing at a rate of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{in}/\\text{min}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =18\\,\\text{in}, \\\\ z & =10\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=540\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}/\\text{min}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ when $y=18\\,\\text{in}$ and $z=10\\,\\text{in}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nV=x(18)(10)=180x.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(180x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =180(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known value into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}540 & =180(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =3\\,\\text{in}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length is increasing at a rate of $3\\,\\text{in}/\\text{min}.$",
